{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-29T16:29:55.004Z","author":"codex","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"3b5e62ebb1f8ac82bae80594","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-29T16:29:55.004Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-29T16:29:55.004Z","author":"codex","text":"2026-09-29 candidate: the disposable Git fixture failed on the previous workflow (new date tag instead of committed v2000.01.02), then passed after the decision resumed that tag. It also verifies a fresh feature gets a new version, later source commits preserve the pending version, and an unrelated manual version bump is refused. npm run release:check passed 219/219 tests, docstring 49/49 declarations across 8 files, audit 0 production vulnerabilities, and attestation gate 1/1 publish path; coverage measured 99.29% lines, 96.68% branches, 100% functions, below the requested 100% floor. pm health --strict-exit fails on two pre-existing merge receipts for pm-linear-unfa and pm-linear-4yle; pm merge reconcile --dry-run reports no_receipt_set_proves_snapshot for both, so neither was forced. Rollback: revert the workflow decision change before any release run; no registry or hosted state was changed by this candidate."}]}],"before_hash":"937e9836d22ff661e5201fdc1457bb80caa67e516bcbb03f9372ed7fd590a5f5","after_hash":"85da9e6e4b909e6552dc46604946985c4c51df64dad9166e3c53030a40a40e17","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Record red-green fixture, exact gate evidence, and rollback","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavai