{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-29T16:40:30.460Z","author":"codex","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"3b5e62ebb1f8ac82bae80594","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-09-29T16:40:30.460Z","author":"codex","text":"Review reconciliation 2026-09-29: Greptile correctly found that a retry after later source commits could tag the newer HEAD for an already-published version. The candidate now refuses that state before emitting release outputs; automatic recovery across a newer main head requires a separate provenance-safe design. Greptile also identified two missing refusal cases; the disposable Git fixture now covers a conflicting tag on unrelated history and a release-subject/package-version mismatch. CodeRabbit correctly found tagger-clock order could select an older release; the workflow now selects the nearest reachable mainline release tag and a skewed-tagger-date fixture exercises it. None of these findings are treated as resolved until exact-head gates and re-review complete."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-29T16:40:30.460Z"}],"before_hash":"7532caa48ccad11df7fba1dd172a9515e0a9a6c65db2e191f02a1b2a0d470db3","after_hash":"f45d73bbe4fe1ecceadbdf8c25cbc536771a2ff844651db653c3930f8ec70f0f","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Record review findings, fixes, and remaining recovery limit","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"reco